# G113 — Web Board / Forum

*v2. See `web-board.md` for prose: parent-pointer tree with derived DFS
walk, signed score from two counters, Reddit-style hot formula,
pinned-first as primary sort override, write-time parent validation.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Discussion Board

[vault-discussion-board @board-path
    IN ORDER TO
        render a forum front page sorted by hot score
        open threads as depth-indented reply trees
        and accept new replies with parent validation

    @board <- [wb[load {path: @board-path}]]

    sync @user-events {
        visit-front-page ->
            @threads <- [wb[list-threads
                              {board: @board, sort: "hot",
                               now-ms: [clock[now]]}]]
            [ui[render-thread-list {threads: @threads}]]

        open-thread @thread-id ->
            @tree <- [wb[thread-tree
                           {board: @board, thread-id: @thread-id}]]
            [ui[render-tree {tree: @tree}]]

        reply @parent-id @body ->
            @parent <- [wb[get-post {board: @board, id: @parent-id}]]
            [wb[add-post
                 {board: @board,
                  post: {thread-id: @parent:thread-id,
                         parent-id: @parent-id,
                         author: @user, body: @body,
                         created-ms: [clock[now]],
                         upvotes: 0, downvotes: 0}}]]
                || -> #invalid-parent @resistance:reason
    }
]

---

## Verb Surface

[wb
    new
    load                  {path}
    add-thread            {board, thread}
    add-post              {board, post}                 ;; || invalid-parent
    get-post              {board, id}                   ;; || not-found
    post-score            {post}                         ;; -> Int (signed)
    hot-score             {post, now-ms}                 ;; -> Float
    thread-tree           {board, thread-id}             ;; -> [PostWithDepth]
    top-level-posts       {board, thread-id}
    children-of           {board, post-id}
    list-threads          {board, sort, now-ms}
    post-count            {board, thread-id}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: parent integrity as `where` at write time

[wb[add-post {board: @b, post: @p}]
    IN ORDER TO
        accept the post only when it fits the board's tree invariants
        so hierarchical data can never drift into nonsense

    @p
        where thread-id exists in @b:threads
        and parent-id
            (is none when this is a top-level post
             or references a post that exists in @b:posts
             and belongs to @p:thread-id)
        || -> #invalid-parent @p
]

Top-level posts are marked by `parent-id: none`, not `parent-id: 0`
or self-reference — `none` is the unambiguous root marker and the
distinction matters when re-serialising the flat store.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: sort order as `where` with pinned override

[wb[list-threads {board: @b, sort: @sort, now-ms: @now}]
    IN ORDER TO
        produce a thread list where moderator-pinned entries sit on top
        and all remaining entries follow the user's chosen sort

    @b:threads
        ordered by
            pinned descending,
            @sort is "new" ? created-ms descending :
            @sort is "top" ? [wb[post-score]] of top post descending :
            @sort is "hot" ? [wb[hot-score {post, now-ms: @now}]] descending
]

`pinned descending` is always the primary sort — the user's choice
only orders within each pinned/unpinned block.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: DFS walk emits depth as first-class output

[wb[thread-tree {board: @b, thread-id: @t}]
    @b:posts
        where thread-id is @t
        depth-first from roots (parent-id is none)
        ordered within each level by created-ms ascending
        yielding each post with its depth
]

Rendering indentation becomes one map: `[indent depth][body]`. No
second pass to re-walk the tree, no layout bookkeeping in the UI.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @b <- [wb[new]]
    [wb[add-thread {board: @b,
                     thread: {id: 1, title: "Welcome",
                               author: "mod", pinned: true,
                               created-ms: 1000000}}]]

    [wb[add-post
         {board: @b,
          post: {id: 10, thread-id: 1, parent-id: none,
                 author: "alice", body: "hi",
                 created-ms: 1000000,
                 upvotes: 10, downvotes: 1}}]]

    [wb[add-post
         {board: @b,
          post: {id: 11, thread-id: 1, parent-id: 10,
                 author: "bob", body: "hi alice",
                 created-ms: 1100000,
                 upvotes: 5, downvotes: 0}}]]

    -> [wb[thread-tree {board: @b, thread-id: 1}]]
    ;; -> [(post 10, depth 0), (post 11, depth 1)]

    -> [wb[post-score {post: [wb[get-post {board: @b, id: 10}]]}]]
    ;; -> 9
]
